WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.160
Speaker 1: And speaking of things that&nbsp;
also make absolutely no sense whatsoever.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:10.400
New reports have revealed that ICE officials&nbsp;
were instructed by the Trump administration&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:21.360
to wipe their cell phones before he left&nbsp;
office. So prior to January 20th of 2021,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:30.240
we have ICE officials. It has now been confirmed,&nbsp;
of course. That deleted all of the data&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:35.600
off of their phones, just like we saw with.
Speaker 2: Members of the Department of Justice.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:38.960
Members of the Department of Homeland Security.
Speaker 1: And, of course, most famously,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:46.240
the United States Secret Service. Everybody just&nbsp;
wiped all their phones, deleted everything off&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:53.520
it. Text messages, emails, notes, games,&nbsp;
whatever. It was totally erased. It all.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:59.280
And even if just like the Secret&nbsp;
Service claimed. Right. Oh,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:04.160
this was just routine. We just. This is a&nbsp;
thing we do. Cool. Totally understand that.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:13.760
You're still required by law to preserve&nbsp;
the data. And that's the big part that I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:21.600
think a lot of people don't quite understand&nbsp;
about this. It is not routine for the DOJ,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:27.280
for the Homeland Security, for the Secret Service&nbsp;
to just wipe everything off the phone and turn it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:33.120
back in and say, all right, thank you. Bye. I'll&nbsp;
see you next time. No, the phones are taken.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:41.680
Inventory is done. They are copied.
Speaker 2: And then they are wiped.&nbsp;

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:48.400
Speaker 1: And this, of course, only applies to&nbsp;
agency issued phones, which most of these people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:56.560
do have agency issued phones, and they have it for&nbsp;
that specific reason so that the data is saved,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.560 --> 00:02:01.280
so that there are records of the things that&nbsp;
they do, the communications that they have,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:06.400
so that they can make sure these individuals&nbsp;
are not sending it to people who shouldn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:11.440
be receiving it. And in case there's&nbsp;
any malfeasance, we can point it out.&nbsp;

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:18.000
Speaker 2: Due to the records on their devices.
Speaker 1: And now we know that ICE,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:24.960
Immigrations and Customs Enforcement wiped&nbsp;
their phones just like so many other government.&nbsp;

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:33.840
Speaker 2: Agencies under Donald Trump.
Speaker 1: I don't know how much more of this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:42.160
we can go through. How many more cell&nbsp;
phones were wiped before Trump left?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:49.440
How many other agencies, how many other officials&nbsp;
were given these orders to scrub it all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:53.920
to get rid of any evidence, get rid of any&nbsp;
trace of anything, make sure nobody knows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:59.760
who we were talking to. And when we were talking&nbsp;
to them and what we were talking to them about.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:10.720
That should terrify you. And every single person&nbsp;
involved needs to be investigated because like I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:20.400
said, it's illegal. To delete these records. They&nbsp;
are required by law to back them up. And I'm not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:27.440
saying go find the IT department and arrest those&nbsp;
guys for wiping their devices. They probably&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:33.120
didn't know that they hadn't been backed up.&nbsp;
Whoever made the call, whoever made the decision&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:38.960
for all of these devices to be wiped at whatever&nbsp;
agency it is we're talking about that day.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:41.760
Those are the people that need.
Speaker 2: To be held accountable.&nbsp;

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:47.840
Speaker 1: And maybe there's a couple honest&nbsp;
folks in there. Maybe some of them backed up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:52.560
their own data. Maybe they understood&nbsp;
that I was just following orders is not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:58.720
necessarily a good excuse for breaking the law.
Speaker 2: So maybe there are records somewhere.&nbsp;

00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:02.640
Speaker 1: Right? Even in the case of the Secret&nbsp;
Service, in all their missing cell phone data,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:06.720
once the investigation was lost, they came&nbsp;
back and magically said, oh, wait, wait,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:13.280
we just found data on ten devices. Look at that.&nbsp;
Wow. Oh, suddenly it's crazy. We may be looking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.280 --> 00:04:20.000
at a situation like that, but only if we put&nbsp;
the pressure on these organizations. And that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:25.029
pressure has to either come from Congress or it&nbsp;
has to come from the Biden administration via the.&nbsp;

00:04:25.029 --> 00:04:27.840
Speaker 2: Department of Justice.&nbsp;
That's what has to happen.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:34.000
Remains to be seen, though,&nbsp;
right? I guess we have to wait.

